{
  "about": "Paztport's Ed25519 vectors: the signature rule (spec wire.md, Signatures) where Ed25519 libraries disagree. Each case gives publicKey, the base64url of the bytes handed to the verifier as an X.509 SPKI (some are not an Ed25519 SPKI), message and signature, base64url of the bytes; valid is the rule's answer. A replay hands the three to the SDK's verify and expects valid; a key the platform refuses to decode counts as not valid. smallOrderY lists the y of every point of small order, each as its 32 little-endian bytes in hex, ascending as numbers: the five values rule 4 refuses, tested on the y of R and A with the sign bit ignored. In the case names, y8 is smallOrderY's fourth value and p - y8 its third. The cases were crafted, and every answer worked out, by RFC 8032 arithmetic written for the generator, which imports no SDK code. Cases may be added; a recorded answer changes only with a protocol change.",
